Hushfacebook combines the Facebook patches of several Morphe patch sources.
Its build, shared extension library and release checks come from Hushfeed,
which is built on icysymmetra/tiktok-patches-for-morphe, which is built on
Morphe, which hard forked ReVanced. Its Facebook patches are rewritten from
Andrew Liang's patches, which credit FroggoMorphePatches for some of their
ideas and implementations, and the feed filter follows FroggoMorphePatches in
also dropping promoted posts. The notices below are reproduced from those
projects. Morphe requires its text to be carried in derivative works and shown
to the person using the software, so it is also reachable in the app itself:
long-press Facebook's launcher icon, open Hushfacebook, then Licenses.

  Hushfacebook                https://github.com/SysAdminDoc/Hushfacebook
  Hushfeed                    https://github.com/SysAdminDoc/hushfeed
  morphe-patches (Andrew's)   https://github.com/andrewliang25/morphe-patches
  FroggoMorphePatches         https://github.com/SapitoSucio/FroggoMorphePatches
  tiktok-patches-for-morphe   https://github.com/icysymmetra/tiktok-patches-for-morphe
  morphe-patches              https://github.com/MorpheApp/morphe-patches
  morphe-patches-library      https://github.com/MorpheApp/morphe-patches-library
  ReVanced                    https://gitlab.com/ReVanced/revanced-patches

Andrew Liang's patches and FroggoMorphePatches are licensed under the GNU
General Public License v3.0. Their files here keep a "Forked from" line naming
the file and commit they came from, and provenance.json records every rule.


